function guide2(){app.innerHTML=`<div class="hud"><button class="hb" onclick="home()">← Back</button><span class="hp">📘 Guide</span></div><div class="card lg" style="margin-top:14px;text-align:left"><div class="sec" style="margin-top:0">🖥️ HOW TECHFIX DESKTOP WORKS</div>
<ol style="padding-left:1.2em;line-height:1.6;font-weight:600">
<li>Open <b>🛠️ GAME</b> and pick a ticket. The ticket tells you the problem the user has.</li>
<li>The simulator opens as a real computer desktop. <b>Rotate your phone sideways</b> if you play on a phone.</li>
<li>Open apps by tapping their icons: Settings, Task Manager, Browser, Files, Router, Command Prompt, Repair Mode, PC Case and Monitor. Drag a window by its title bar. Tap ✕ to close it.</li>
<li>Think like a technician: <b>SEE</b> the symptoms · <b>THINK</b> about the possible causes · <b>TRY</b> the safest fix first · <b>CHECK</b> that the problem is gone.</li>
<li>Stuck? Tap <b>💡 Hint</b>. Hints cost points.</li>
<li>Score: each problem starts at 100 points. Every wrong try costs 10 points and every hint costs 5 points. The lowest score is 30. ★★★ = 90 or more · ★★ = 70 or more · ★ = less.</li>
<li>After each solved problem you answer a <b>quick quiz</b>. The quiz does not change your problem score.</li>
<li>Tap <b>EXIT</b> to leave. Your progress on the problem you are solving is not saved.</li></ol></div>
<div class="card lg" style="text-align:left"><div class="sec" style="margin-top:0">🔬 ABOUT THE STUDY</div><p style="line-height:1.55;font-weight:600">The order is: <b>1. Pre-Test → 2. Game → 3. Post-Test → 4. Usability Survey</b>. The Post-Test opens after you solve at least ${MIN_PER_TOPIC} problems in every topic. Game points are only for practice and fun. The research result is based on your pre-test and post-test scores, not on your game points.</p></div><div style="text-align:center;margin:14px"><button class="btn" onclick="home()">OK</button></div>`}

